            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0338" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1830: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-06T23:00:00-04:00">March 6, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Your 51, February 28, 12 a.m. and 54, March 3, noon.<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d377-f1"/> As soon as possible after the formation of a new cabinet
                    it is requested that you see the Prime Minister and discuss with him courteously
                    but firmly the question of the continued presence in Iran of Japanese diplomatic
                    and consular representatives. In that discussion you should point out that the
                    presence of these officials is a grave danger not only to the interests of the
                    United States and its associates in the war against aggression but also to Iran
                    itself. In this latter connection you should stress the fact that fifth column
                    activities of Japanese officials have played an important part in subjugating
                    those countries in Asia which Japan has temporarily overrun. Accordingly you
                    should express the strong conviction of this Government that the best interests
                    of Iran require the prompt severance of relations with Japan.</p>
                <p>Please keep me promptly informed of developments in this matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
